      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Cases with foreign bodies in the bladder are rarely seen. According to literature, it has been reported that foreign bodies were removed from the bladder. The etiology of these cases are iatrogenic causes, migration from adjacent organs, tissues and self-insertion. In this case report, we presented a 22-year-old female who was admitted to the emergency room with vaginal bleeding, and groin pain. The foreign body was removed from the urinary bladder."},
